* sw3157.lib: open behavioural models of a 3157-class SPDT analog switch used as an SPST (COM to the low-selected
* throw), and of the TMUX1119 for comparison, at a 3.3 V supply.  Written for this project (whatif/sw3157); our own
* work, not a vendor model and containing none.  Licence: CC BY-SA 4.0 (LICENSE beside this file), (c) the project authors.
* Generated by make_lib.py (beside this file) from the digitised curves quoted there; curves.json holds them as data.
*
* Sources (vendor files, git-ignored, fetched and hash-checked by tools/fetch_models.py from models/manifest.json):
*   74lvc1g3157/74lvc1g3157.pdf  Nexperia 74LVC1G3157 Rev. 11 (23 Aug 2023)
*   ts5a3157/ts5a3157.pdf        TI TS5A3157 SCDS219D (Jul 2025)
*   tmux1119/tmux1119.pdf        TI TMUX1119 SCDS401C (Feb 2024)
*
* Closed switch: Ron(V) = rpk - flat + flat * s(Vc), Vc = mean of the two pin voltages (the drop across the switch is
* tens of mV here), s() the normalised shape (0..1 over 0-3.3 V) of a digitised typical curve:
*   SHAPE NX : Nexperia Fig. 10 (p. 8), VCC 3.3 V, 25 C; raw 5.757-7.698 ohm (min at 1.6 V, max at 2.4 V),
*              flatness 1.94 ohm against Table 8's typical 2.0 (ISW 24 mA, VCC 3-3.6 V).  Reading error about +/-0.05 ohm.
*   SHAPE TM : TMUX1119 Figure 5-1 (p. 9), mean of the VDD = 3 V and 3.63 V curves; raw 1.996-4.105 ohm.
*              The table (Sec 5.6, p. 5) gives RON 3.7 typ / 8.8 max and RON_FLAT 1.9 typ at 25 C.
* The TS5A3157 publishes no curve: its corners below use the NX shape *(assumption: a 3157-class shape, not TI's)*.
* Vc is clamped to 0-3.3 V (the digitised span) and Ron to at least 0.1 ohm, so that Newton iterations far from the
* solution never see a negative resistance.
* On capacitance con is split con/2 to ground at each pin; il is a leakage current from each pin to ground.
*
* Corners (rpk, flat) used by whatif/sw3157 (every one quoted from the datasheet unless marked):
*   74LVC1G3157 typ 25 C    rpk 7.698 flat 1.941  (the digitised curve itself)
*   74LVC1G3157 max         rpk 20   flat 5.04  RON(peak) max 20 ohm (Table 8, -40..85 C, VCC 3-3.6 V); RON(flat) has no
*                           maximum, so the curve is scaled x 20/7.698 *(assumption: proportional scaling)*
*   TS5A3157 typ 25 C       rpk 12   flat 8     (Sec 5.5 p. 6, V+ = 3 V, rON typ 12, ron(flat) typ 8)
*   TS5A3157 max 25 C       rpk 20   flat 13    (rON max 20, ron(flat) max 13); Full (-40..85 C): rpk 20 flat 14
*   either 3157, literal bound rpk 20 flat 0  (Ron at its 20 ohm maximum everywhere: the datasheet bound as written)
*   TMUX1119 typ 25 C       rpk 3.7  flat 1.9   (Sec 5.6 p. 5);  max: rpk 8.8, flat 2.2 (the -40..125 C flatness figure)
* NOT modelled: temperature (use the corners; NX tabulates its four curves in make_lib.py), Ron against current (the
* tables are at 10-30 mA, this circuit carries at most about 6 mA), body diodes (add DESD at the pins where needed),
* break-before-make and charge injection (TS5A3157 3 pC, Nexperia 5.0 pC at 3.3 V, TMUX1119 -6 pC).
*
.subckt RSWV_NX a b params: rpk=7.698 flat=1.941 con=18p il=0
Bsw a b I = V(a,b)/max({rpk-flat} + {flat}*pwl(min(max((V(a)+V(b))/2, 0), 3.3), 0.0,0.3524, 0.1,0.3946, 0.2,0.4384, 0.3,0.4941, 0.4,0.5544, 0.5,0.6193, 0.6,0.6847, 0.7,0.7264, 0.8,0.7032, 0.9,0.5914, 1.0,0.4199, 1.1,0.3014, 1.2,0.1808, 1.3,0.0994, 1.4,0.0371, 1.5,0.0046, 1.6,0.0000, 1.7,0.0185, 1.8,0.0716, 1.9,0.1556, 2.0,0.3199, 2.1,0.4781, 2.2,0.7682, 2.3,0.9768, 2.4,1.0000, 2.5,0.8815, 2.6,0.7728, 2.7,0.6589, 2.8,0.5523, 2.9,0.4616, 3.0,0.3663, 3.1,0.3040, 3.2,0.2318, 3.3,0.1880), 0.1)
Con1 a 0 {con/2}
Con2 b 0 {con/2}
Ila a 0 {il}
Ilb b 0 {il}
.ends
.subckt RSWV_TM a b params: rpk=7.698 flat=1.941 con=18p il=0
Bsw a b I = V(a,b)/max({rpk-flat} + {flat}*pwl(min(max((V(a)+V(b))/2, 0), 3.3), 0.0,0.0000, 0.1,0.0491, 0.2,0.0984, 0.3,0.1472, 0.4,0.2010, 0.5,0.2568, 0.6,0.3276, 0.7,0.4099, 0.8,0.5031, 0.9,0.6128, 1.0,0.7378, 1.1,0.8651, 1.2,0.9061, 1.3,0.8969, 1.4,0.8777, 1.5,0.8857, 1.6,0.9170, 1.7,0.9694, 1.8,1.0000, 1.9,0.9896, 2.0,0.9256, 2.1,0.8423, 2.2,0.7494, 2.3,0.6399, 2.4,0.5465, 2.5,0.4616, 2.6,0.3860, 2.7,0.3182, 2.8,0.2584, 2.9,0.2082, 3.0,0.1622, 3.1,0.1133, 3.2,0.0721, 3.3,0.0256), 0.1)
Con1 a 0 {con/2}
Con2 b 0 {con/2}
Ila a 0 {il}
Ilb b 0 {il}
.ends
* open switch: coff across the open path (conservative for the +/-1.25 V pole; the datasheets give the off capacitance
* of a pin to ground, not across the switch) and a leakage current from each pin
.subckt RSWV_OPEN a b params: coff=6p il=0
Coff a b {coff}
Ila a 0 {il}
Ilb b 0 {il}
.ends
